## Requirements

- **Node.js:** `v18.20.5`
- **npm:** comes with Node.js

You can verify your Node.js version by running:

```bash
node -v
```

Expected output:

```text
v18.20.5
```

---

## Installation

1. Clone this repository
2. Open the terminal and navigate to the project directory
3. Checkout to the `main` brunch
4. Install the dependencies using npm: `npm ci` or `npm install` or `npm i`

## Running the App

After successfully installing the dependencies, you can run the app. Use the following command:
`npm start`
This command will start the development server. You can open the app in your browser at http://localhost:3000.

## Development

All project files are located in the src directory. You can edit these files to modify the behavior of the app.

## Building

If you're ready to deploy your app for production use, run the following command:
`npm run build`
This command will build the project and create an optimized version of the app in the build directory. You can deploy this version to your server.
